From: Soe Thura <6492082+thixpin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:29:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] Enter functions at secondary entry points

A direct branch or call to an address inside another function has no translation target, and a
call target inside a function was analysed again as an overlapping function. Forza Motorsport 4
has 85 such targets: tails shared between functions and code without .pdata that the sweep
splits. Each is now a secondary entry, sub_<address>, emitted as the containing function's
body entered with a goto after the declarations, with a NOTE line. Calls into known functions
no longer create functions; functions found by analysis end at the next function, and the sweep
never runs over it. A branch to a zero word of a code section outside any function is an
illegal instruction and traps. In test mode, functions are declared before use and secondary
entries are emitted.
---
